{
  "case_id": "2008-07-582",
  "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Solicitor General Garre (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL GARRE: They did change the policy, Justice Scalia, and the Commission directly acknowledged that in paragraph 12 of the Golden Globe Awards order, which is not reprinted in the petition appendix. In that paragraph, the Commission said, \"We now depart from cases holding that isolated or fleeting use of the F-Word was not indecent.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, is the agency's position that its policy has changed or that it has not changed?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: One of the problems is that, seeing it in operation, there seems to be no rhyme or reason for some of the decisions that the Commission has made. I mean, the \"Saving Private Ryan\" case was filled with expletives, and yet the film about jazz history, the words were considered a violation of the Commission's policies."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Solicitor General Garre (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL GARRE: Well, first of all, the community standards are community standards for the broadcast medium. This is set out a little bit at page 33 of the joint appendix at footnote 13. Second of all, they look to community standards for the average listener. And, third of all, the -- the Commission applies its expressly -- collective experience here, looking to statements from lawmakers, from courts, from broadcasters, from public interest groups, and from citizens to determine what is consistent with community standards."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: So, what is it -- what are they supposed to do when the event is live, and lo and behold, they have a few people in front of them who swear, using these words? What is their -- what can they do?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Garre (FCC)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL GARRE: In a show like the Billboard\nMusic Awards, they will use a delay. And since the\nincidents in this case, the 2003 and 2002 instances, the\nnetworks have gotten more people who are on hand to\nbleep isolated expletives."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Did the FCC explain all\nthis in its opinion when it said, we understand that now\nwe're going to have to -- every incident is going to\nhave to be -- have a 5-second delay and they will have\nto have tapes, and we think it's worth the cost? Did\nthey explain all that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: It depends on whom you are\ndealing with, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Garre (FCC)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL GARRE: Certainly our view is that\nit was pandering and invited. It could have been\nexpected."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Garre (FCC)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL GARRE: We did not fine them because\nwe exercised restraint in making -- in attempting to\nmake clear that the FCC going forward was going to\nconsider isolated --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Garre (FCC)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0001-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL GARRE: Yes, insofar as the\nCommission takes into account whether it's shocking,\ntitillating, pandering --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: May I just ask one\nquestion? It's about the bottom line of your brief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Garre (FCC)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0001-0010",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL GARRE: Well, that approach would be\nconsistent with this Court not deciding issues that\nhaven't been decided below and the general practice of\nconstitutional avoidance."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Could that be -- could\nthat be done without deciding this APA or are we forced\nto decide that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Are they -- are they\nsupposed to be more virtuous than courts?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Well, one thing has\nchanged. One thing has changed, I think, from the\nrecord. And let me ask you whether if the Commission\nhad given this explanation it would in your judgment\nsatisfy the arbitrary and capricious standard?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: How is that consistent with Vermont Yankee?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Phillips",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I am asking for a higher standard under the APA because we are talking about content-based restrictions on free speech."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: If there is -- if there is a change in the community standards, does that justify a change in the FCC's policies?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "National Association of Broadcasters",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0002-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the NAB amicus brief actually has a pretty good description of a variety of different instances in which this has -- has occurred."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: -- does the -- does the number of times the word is used in a particular context make a difference in the definition?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: As a matter of statutory definition, if a particular word can describe those activities, it is equally indecent if used for a different purpose?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Let me ask about deferring there."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Could I ask one question that just occurred to me? Do you think the use of the word dung, D-U-N-G, would be indecent?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Garre",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bba080d3f96a-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The one thing that can't be disputed -- in this case is that the F-Word is patently offensive under community standards for the broadcast medium."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2008-07-582",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "bba080d3f96a4307047d97362f9f79a71745b5bac0325bdab9fab66d50475bac",
